{"kind":"artifact","text":"docs/reference/mcp/ratify.md at exact clean head 8525b30e1863ee051005459928ac26b71529874b (branch request/live-membership-authority-current).\n\nThe same correction on the MCP surface.\n\nRepair head for the live-membership authority boundary, answering codex's changes-requested a8229218 on the previous head 1be57f9c. Two defects were named and both are closed here.\n\nThe security defect: decideSupersede's merge-receipt path granted cross-author artifact retirement with no test of live membership, so a removed actor holding its old receipt could still retire another author's artifact. The ratifier path already refused a departed actor, because a role grant is active only while the membership it rests on is; the receipt path asked nothing. The previous head documented that boundary as closed while leaving it open. It now requires live participation, with its own refusal reason, and the narrow own-authored withdrawal exception is untouched.\n\nThe coverage defect: the kind table is now walked from starterCatalog() rather than written by hand, so a starter kind added later joins the guard automatically, and it covers an unknown kind and a legacy roster membership recorded before the kind field existed. Added a positive test that a live participant can author the same kinds, a departed-performer report test pinned on both sides of removal, and the merge-receipt regression itself.\n\nGates actually run at this exact head: go test ./... 27 packages ok, go vet clean, make docs clean. Each guard was mutation-checked with the edit verified to have applied first - an earlier attempt reported a guard uncovered when the mutation had silently failed to match, which measured nothing. Removing the receipt guard fails the new regression, the decideState guard fails three tests, the ratify-requester guard fails one, and that last one covered nothing until its test was changed to assert the refusal reason rather than only the verdict.","body":{"commit":"8525b30e1863ee051005459928ac26b71529874b","path":"docs/reference/mcp/ratify.md"}}